"""patch_g4_addendum1_1030.py (2026-10-30): appends Addendum 1 (the recall check, the volatility-table gap and Part B2) to results/PREREG_g4_price_artifacts_2026-10-30.md.
The registration must be exactly the committed version (sha256 c73d7dd3...) or nothing is changed. The text before PRED-TABLE-END is compared before and after: no registered prediction is edited."""
import hashlib, sys
def sha(s): return hashlib.sha256((s if s.endswith("\n") else s + "\n").encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()
p = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "results/PREREG_g4_price_artifacts_2026-10-30.md"
T = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read()
assert sha(T) == "c73d7dd39fda15d7cf2e576df5eddee9e3e161f4333211b611baf0ada3fddfad", "the registration is not the committed version; nothing changed"
new = """
ADDENDUM 1 (2026-10-30, after S0 to S5, the review and the recall check; BEFORE Part B2 was listed): FINDINGS. (a) RECALL CHECK against the old scan of 2026-10-28: HIG 2008-12-05 (+102.4 percent, v64 0.1663, z 5.97), ROK 2001-07-02 (-61.4 percent), HUBB 1994-10-31 (+886 percent) and TSCO 1994-02-18 (+225 percent) are NOT in Part B: one misses the z cutoff of 6 by 0.03 in the crisis, three have no v64. The three registered positive controls (KDP, KLAC, HPQ) were caught (p7 true), but the registered design was NOT a superset of the old scan, which had no volatility requirement: this is a flaw of the registration, not of the data. (b) THE VOLATILITY TABLE HAS GAPS: of the non-sealed price rows, vol_estimators has v64 for 0.0 percent of the rows of 1994 and of every year from 1998 to 2003 (400,277 rows, 17.6 percent of the 2,275,434), for 97.1 to 97.8 percent in 1995 to 1997, for 98.0 to 99.9 percent in 2004 to 2025 and for 89.3 percent in 2026 (the table ends 2026-09-15). This is recorded as a data limitation (for G8 and for any analysis that reads v64); G4 does not build volatility estimates. (c) COUNTS of non-sealed one-day adjusted moves of 30 percent or more, by band, as days / v64 missing / in Part B / v64 present with z below 6: 30 to 40 percent 182 / 69 / 62 / 51; 40 to 60 percent 55 / 20 / 22 / 13; 60 to 100 percent 11 / 4 / 7 / 0; 100 percent or more 5 / 2 / 2 / 1; Part B holds 93 of the 253 days. PART B2 (added): a B2 day is a one-day adjusted move of 30 percent or more that is not a Part B candidate. B2a: every B2 day with a move of 60 percent or more (7 days by the counts), reviewed in full. B2b: B2 days with a move of 30 to 60 percent (153 by the counts): a sample of 40 in the fixed order of md5(ticker and date), and if 3 or more of the 40 are artifacts (7.5 percent) ALL 153 are reviewed. The statements are in scripts/sql/g4_scan_b2_2026-10-30.sql; the labels, the evidence and the confirmation by Galen of every item work exactly as in the STANDARD TEST, and the PASS TEST item (2) now also covers B2a and B2b. REVIEW SO FAR (decisions of Galen, 2026-10-30): confirmed artifacts 9 (KDP 2018-07-10, KLAC 2014-11-26, HPQ 2015-11-02, A 2014-11-03, MO 2008-03-31, CAH 2009-09-01, JCI 2007-07-02, DD 2019-06-03, GEN 2020-02-03); NEEDS EVIDENCE 26 (WY 2010-07-20, EXPE 2011-12-21, MAS 2015-07-01, GIS 1995-05-30, MGM 2004-05-18; the lean DPZ 2007-05-07, LH 1997-12-22, MGM 2008-07-10; and the 18 uncertain rows); the real groups were accepted. PREDICTIONS ADDED HERE (the PRED-TABLE is not edited; these are scored by hand in the results file): (p12) at least 4 of the 7 B2a days are labeled artifact, probability 0.70; (p13) the share of the 40 B2b sample labeled artifact is 5 percent, 80 percent interval 0 to 15 percent. NOT DONE BY THIS ADDENDUM: no exclusion is applied; the 9 events whose windows contain a confirmed artifact and are still in the analysis set (A 2014-10-06, 2014-10-14 and 2014-11-03; CAH 2009-08-27 and 2009-09-01; DD 2019-05-23, 2019-05-29 and 2019-06-03; GEN 2020-01-09) are PROPOSED for event_exclusions (reason price_step_in_window) and wait for Galen to approve each.
"""
head = T[:T.index("PRED-TABLE-END")]
R = T.rstrip("\n") + "\n" + new
assert R[:R.index("PRED-TABLE-END")] == head
open(p, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(R)
R2 = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read(); print("ok   Addendum 1 appended"); print("registration sha256", sha(R2), "|", R2.count("\n"), "lines")
